/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_TypeTraits Type Traits
 * @ingroup Foundation
 * @brief Compile-time type inspection and relationships for generic code.
 *
 * TypeTraits provides small, allocation-free compile-time utilities with an API
 * shaped like the corresponding C++ standard-library traits. A trait exposes a
 * compile-time `value`; C++17 consumers may use its shorter `_v` form.
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <Foundation_TypeTraits.h>
 *
 * using namespace Foundation::TypeTraits;
 *
 * static_assert(is_integral<int>::value, "int must be integral");
 * static_assert(is_pointer_v<const char*>, "expected a pointer");
 * static_assert(is_same_v<remove_cv<const int>::type, int>,
 *               "remove_cv must remove top-level qualifiers");
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationTypeTraitsHeaders Public Headers
 *
 * Prefer one of these supported entry points:
 *
 * | Need | Header |
 * | ---- | ------ |
 * | Entire Foundation library | `#include <Foundation.h>` |
 * | Entire TypeTraits module | `#include <Foundation_TypeTraits.h>` |
 * | Nested module umbrella | `#include <Foundation/TypeTraits.h>` |
 * | One trait family only | `#include <Foundation/TypeTraits/<Family>.h>` |
 *
 * The top-level and nested module umbrellas expose the same TypeTraits surface.
 * Selective family headers are useful on embedded targets when minimizing
 * parsed declarations matters.
 *
 * @section FoundationTypeTraitsFamilies Trait Families
 *
 * | Family | Purpose | Representative traits |
 * | ------ | ------- | --------------------- |
 * | @ref Foundation_TypeTraits_Helpers "Helper classes" | Store a typed compile-time value. | `integral_constant`, `bool_constant`, `true_type`, `false_type` |
 * | @ref Foundation_TypeTraits_Properties "Type properties and transformations" | Inspect qualifiers and transform a type. | `is_const`, `is_volatile`, `is_unsigned`, `remove_cv` |
 * | @ref Foundation_TypeTraits_Primary "Primary categories" | Classify one fundamental kind of type. | `is_integral`, `is_pointer`, `is_class`, `is_function` |
 * | @ref Foundation_TypeTraits_Composite "Composite categories" | Combine primary classifications. | `is_arithmetic`, `is_scalar`, `is_object`, `is_reference`, `is_unsigned_integer` |
 * | @ref Foundation_TypeTraits_Relationships "Type relationships" | Compare types or expressions. | `is_same`, `is_base_of`, `is_convertible`, `is_invocable` |
 *
 * @section FoundationTypeTraitsSurface Supported v1 Surface
 *
 * | Family | Supported names |
 * | ------ | --------------- |
 * | Helpers | `integral_constant`, `bool_constant`, `true_type`, `false_type` |
 * | Transformations | `remove_const`, `remove_volatile`, `remove_cv`, and their `_t` aliases |
 * | Properties | `is_const`, `is_volatile`, `is_unsigned` |
 * | Primary categories | `is_array`, `is_class`, `is_enum`, `is_floating_point`, `is_function`, `is_integral`, `is_lvalue_reference`, `is_member_function_pointer`, `is_member_object_pointer`, `is_pointer`, `is_rvalue_reference`, `is_union`, `is_void` |
 * | Composite categories | `is_arithmetic`, `is_compound`, `is_fundamental`, `is_member_pointer`, `is_object`, `is_reference`, `is_scalar`, `is_unsigned_integer` |
 * | Relationships | `is_same`, `is_base_of`, `is_convertible`, `is_invocable`, `is_nothrow_invocable`, `is_nothrow_convertible` |
 *
 * Every predicate has a C++17 `_v` convenience variable. The supported
 * integral set is the standard C++17 set through `char16_t`, `char32_t`, and
 * `unsigned long long`; compiler-specific extended integers are outside the
 * v1 contract.
 * `is_unsigned_integer` is a Foundation-specific composite trait that combines
 * `is_integral` and `is_unsigned` while excluding `bool`; it is intended for
 * numeric counters and storage representations.
 *
 * @section FoundationTypeTraitsPatterns Usage Patterns
 *
 * Traits may guard a complete generic type:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * template <typename T>
 * class NumericBuffer {
 *     static_assert(
 *         Foundation::TypeTraits::is_arithmetic_v<T>,
 *         "NumericBuffer requires an arithmetic type"
 *     );
 * };
 * @endcode
 *
 * They may also select code without creating runtime state:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * template <typename T>
 * constexpr bool CanStoreByValue() {
 *     return Foundation::TypeTraits::is_scalar_v<T>;
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * Every available `_v` name is a C++17 inline variable equivalent to reading the
 * corresponding trait's `::value`. The class form remains useful when a trait
 * type must be inherited from or passed to another metaprogram.
 *
 * @section FoundationTypeTraitsContract Current Contract
 *
 * - The project language baseline is C++17, so the documented `_v` forms are
 *   available on supported builds.
 * - Traits are evaluated at compile time and do not allocate memory.
 * - Foundation automatically uses the C++ standard `<type_traits>` backend
 *   when the header and the required C++17 invocation traits are available.
 * - Toolchains without that standard-library support use Foundation's local
 *   fallback implementation. The public Foundation trait types and names stay
 *   identical regardless of the selected backend.
 * - `remove_const`, `remove_volatile`, and `remove_cv` remove top-level
 *   qualifiers and expose the result as a nested `type`.
 * - Function classification includes variadic, cv-qualified, ref-qualified,
 *   and `noexcept` function types.
 * - Invocation checks support functions, function objects, member functions,
 *   and member objects through direct objects, pointers, dereferenceable
 *   wrappers, and reference-wrapper-like `get()` access.
 * - `is_nothrow_convertible` is intentionally available under the C++17
 *   baseline even though the similarly named standard trait was added later.
 * - The API uses standard-style lowercase names intentionally; this is the
 *   documented naming exception to Foundation's normal PascalCase type style.
 * - Include a public Foundation header instead of depending on transitive
 *   includes or implementation files.
 *
 * Backend selection is an implementation detail and requires no consumer
 * configuration. The conformance suite compiles every supported trait twice on
 * desktop hosts: once through `<type_traits>` and once through the forced local
 * fallback. Both routes are checked against the standard C++17 results.
 *
 * @section FoundationTypeTraitsExample Runnable Example
 *
 * The `Foundation_TypeTraits_BasicChecks` example demonstrates type
 * classification, relationships, compile-time constraints, and a numeric
 * buffer shared by the desktop executable and Arduino sketch. See
 * @ref FoundationExamplesTypeTraits "TypeTraits BasicChecks" and
 * @ref Foundation_Examples "Examples" for build and launch instructions.
 */

/**
 * @namespace Foundation::TypeTraits
 * @ingroup Foundation_TypeTraits
 * @brief Public namespace for Foundation compile-time type utilities.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_TypeTraits_Helpers Helper Classes
 * @ingroup Foundation_TypeTraits
 * @brief Typed compile-time constants used as trait results.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_TypeTraits_Properties Type Properties and Transformations
 * @ingroup Foundation_TypeTraits
 * @brief Qualifier inspection, signedness inspection, and type transformations.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_TypeTraits_Primary Primary Type Categories
 * @ingroup Foundation_TypeTraits
 * @brief Traits that identify one primary category of a type.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_TypeTraits_Composite Composite Type Categories
 * @ingroup Foundation_TypeTraits
 * @brief Traits composed from multiple primary classifications.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_TypeTraits_Relationships Type Relationships
 * @ingroup Foundation_TypeTraits
 * @brief Traits that compare types or test whether an expression is valid.
 */
